[#207ae]"],"description":"Ocassionally active neurons and neurons that generate bursts will cause the motors to move at random intervals.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775509444086","neuronKeys":["[#dd0de]"],"edgeStrings":["[#e3a8c]_#_[#dd0de]","[#dd0de]_#_[#07e41]","[#dd0de]_#_[#de24f]"],"description":"When SpikerBot gets to close to something, it backs up to not get caught in a difficult situation.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775508692070","neuronKeys":["[#94d4f]"],"edgeStrings":["[#4fead]_#_[#94d4f]"],"description":"This neuron will fire as long as it sees a person. We can use this to have SpikerBot stop to have a quick chat.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775508772881","neuronKeys":["[#94d4f]","[#bebdc]","[#9603f]"],"edgeStrings":["[#94d4f]_#_[#9603f]","[#94d4f]_#_[#bebdc]","[#9603f]_#_[#bebdc]","[#bebdc]_#_[#6cf10]"],"description":"These three neurons produce Feed Forward Inhibition. When SpikerBot first sees a person, it outputs a greeting saying \u2018Ciao\u2019 and then the signalis inhibited while the person is present.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775508832874","neuronKeys":["[#9603f]","[#94d4f]","[#81841]","[#207ae]","[#d328a]","[#c73da]"],"edgeStrings":["[#9603f]_#_[#81841]","[#94d4f]_#_[#9603f]","[#4fead]_#_[#94d4f]","[#9603f]_#_[#207ae]","[#9603f]_#_[#d328a]","[#9603f]_#_[#c73da]"],"description":"As long as we see a person, we can stop exploring, and other unwanted behaviors.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775508884758","neuronKeys":["[#d328a]","[#9a19a]","[#9603f]","[#94d4f]"],"edgeStrings":["[#9603f]_#_[#d328a]","[#d328a]_#_[#9a19a]","[#94d4f]_#_[#9603f]","[#4fead]_#_[#94d4f]"],"description":"When we see a person, we can stop the inhibitory response, allowing the final neuron in this chain to become active!","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775508944966","neuronKeys":["[#9a19a]"],"edgeStrings":["[#b5f52]_#_[#9a19a]"],"description":"This neuron can listen into a conversation. If you speak or make noise, SpikerBot can respond!","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775509017795","neuronKeys":["[#9a19a]"],"edgeStrings":["[#da869]_#_[#6cf10]","[#9a19a]_#_[#da869]","[#b5f52]_#_[#9a19a]","[#f7f98]_#_[#207ae]","[#da869]_#_[#3535d]"],"description":"After a brief delay, Spikerbot will reply \u2018mhmm!\u2019 And light up when it speaks.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775509132460","neuronKeys":["[#da869]","[#f7d43]","[#55942]","[#9a19a]"],"edgeStrings":["[#da869]_#_[#f7d43]","[#da869]_#_[#55942]","[#f7d43]_#_[#9a19a]","[#55942]_#_[#9a19a]"],"description":"When SpikerBot is talking, it sends a few signals to prevent it from listening! Sometimes it can still hear itself. You can experiment to improve SpikerBot\u2019s listening skills!","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775509223356","neuronKeys":["[#c73da]","[#9603f]","[#94d4f]"],"edgeStrings":["[#9603f]_#_[#c73da]","[#94d4f]_#_[#9603f]","[#4fead]_#_[#94d4f]"],"description":"When you finish speaking to SpikerBot, you can say goodbye, and exit so it cannot see you. When you do the last neuron in this chain - set to highly active - can begin to fire again and again.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775509332389","neuronKeys":["[#c73da]","[#b0676]","[#89976]"],"edgeStrings":["[#c73da]_#_[#89976]","[#c73da]_#_[#b0676]","[#b0676]_#_[#89976]","[#89976]_#_[#6cf10]"],"description":"When the highly active parent neuron starts to spike, we use Feed Forward Inhibition again, and SpikerBot yells \u2018Yeehaw!\u2019 once as it gets ready to explore again.","thumbnail":""}],"info":{"title":"Cowboy Stops to Chat","description":"Cowboy explores the west, then stops to have a chat!","author":"User","version":"1.0.1","timestamp":"2026-04-07T19:50:21.807154"}}